profession.description:
A profession represent a type of job practiced in the company. Examples may be:
  - Software engineering ;
  - Consulting ;
  - HR operations ;
  - Finances ;
  - Sales ;
  - etc...

schema.description:
JSON schema of the attribute value. [Read more about employee attribute definition schemas](/api-reference/2024-11-01/employee-attributes/attribute-definition-schemas).

The schema embeds the base schema it is built on, identified by its `$id`, e.g.:
```json
{
  "schema": {
    "$id": "/lucca-api/schemas/taxonomy-label-reference",
    "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
    "title": "taxonomy-label-reference",
    "type": ["object", "null"],
    "additionalProperties": false,
    "required": ["id"],
    "properties": {
        "id": {
            "type": "string",
            "minLength": 1
        },
        "type": {
            "type": "string",
            "const": "taxonomy-label",
            "readOnly": true
        },
        "url": {
            "type": "string",
            "format": "uri",
            "readOnly": true
        }
    }
  }
}
```

Definitions based on the same base schema all embed it with the same `$id`, and identical `$id`s always denote identical schemas. If you register these schemas in a JSON Schema validator (e.g. to validate values before writing them), register each `$id` once: registering it again makes validators such as Ajv fail with a "schema already exists" error.

employee-attribute.description:
An employee-attribute represents a single property value of an employee or any of their directly related resources.

It can be:
- a property of the [employee](/api-reference/2024-11-01/employees/employee) resource;
- a property of their [employment](/api-reference/2024-11-01/employments/employment) resources;
- a property of their [job-position](/api-reference/2024-11-01/employments/job-position) resource;
- an extension property of any of these resources, either user-defined or application-defined.

Such representation makes it possible to retrieve all attributes of an employee in a uniform manner.

